# The graphics show only events, order and labels the notes give.

=== Introduction
--- Post-Tribulation, Pre-Wrath Eschatological Timeline [title]
overline: Prophecy & the covenants
heading: Post-Tribu­lation, Pre-Wrath Eschato­logical Timeline
sub: Based on a 7-Year Framework with a 75-Day Climactic Great Tribulation
refs: Daniel 9:27; Daniel 12:11-12; Matthew 24:29-31; Revelation 6:12-17; Revelation 13:7
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

--- A post-tribulation, pre-wrath view
lead: This document synthesizes a post-tribulation, pre-wrath rapture view of end-times events, grounded in a plain reading of the King James Version (KJV) scriptures. The timeline spans a 7-year period (Daniel’s “one week”), divided into approximately 3.5 years of general tribulation, a 75-day climactic great tribulation, and a period of God’s wrath, culminating in Christ’s return with glorified saints to establish the millennial kingdom.
p: The Book of Revelation is structured as two parallel accounts (chapters 4-11 and 12-22) of the same events, with tribulation in Revelation 6-7 and 13, and wrath in the trumpets (Revelation 8-9) and vials (Revelation 16). This view refutes pre-tribulationism’s conflation of tribulation and wrath and its invention of “tribulation saints,” affirming the church’s presence during tribulation.

--- Overview of the Timeline
- **7-Year Framework:** Derived from [[Daniel 9:27]]’s “one week,” split at the midpoint by the **abomination of desolation** and the **beast’s deadly wound/healing**.
p: **Key Periods:**
panel: First 3.5 Years (~1260 days) | General tribulation (natural and manmade trials, beast’s rise).
panel: 75 Days | Climactic great tribulation, **post-abomination** and **beast’s wound/healing**, marked by the beast’s head wound, dragon empowerment, and intense persecution, “cut short” for the elect ([[Daniel 12:11-12]]’s 1290-1335 days).
panel-warn: Wrath Period | Post-rapture, God’s judgments (trumpets and vials) on the **beast’s kingdom** while the **beast continues his full 42-month reign**, followed by Christ’s return with saints.

--- The rapture, and Revelation’s structure
kicker: Overview of the Timeline
- **Rapture:** Occurs post-tribulation at Christ’s visible second coming ([[Matthew 24:29-31]]), after the 75-day climax (**~1290 days from the abomination**), **before wrath**.
- **Revelation’s Structure:** Chapters 4-11 (heavenly perspective) and 12-22 (cosmic/earthly perspective) overlap, with tribulation in Revelation 6-7 and 13, rapture in [[Revelation 6:12-17]] and [[Revelation 15:2]], and wrath in Revelation 8-9 and 16.

--- The order of events
kicker: Chronological Timeline
image: lessons/prophecy/post-trib-pre-wrath-order.svg | The order of events: covenant confirmed; seals 1 to 5; midpoint at day 1260, the abomination and the beast’s wound healed; 75 days of great tribulation cut short; the sixth seal, sun black, moon blood, stars fall; the rapture; the seventh seal and half-hour silence; wrath in the trumpets and vials; Christ returns with saints at day 2520 | Tribulation, then the rapture, then wrath ([[Matthew 24:29-31]]; [[Revelation 6:12-17]]; [[Revelation 8:1]])

=== 1. General tribulation
--- First 3.5 Years: General Tribulation
kicker: 1 · ~1260 Days
p: **Description:** The 7-year period begins with a covenant, likely involving Israel, initiating tribulation—natural and manmade trials including wars, famines, and persecution. The beast rises, setting the stage for its dominance. The church endures these trials, refuting pre-tribulationism’s early rapture.
p: **Key Events:**
- Covenant confirmed, starting the 7 years.
- Wars, famines, and death afflict the world (Revelation’s early seals).
- Believers face persecution; the beast gains influence.

--- The covenant for one week
kicker: 1 · Scriptures
scripture: Daniel 9:27 | mark: he shall confirm the covenant with many for one week
p: The covenant marks the 7-year start, with the midpoint (~1260 days) pivotal.

--- The first four seals
kicker: 1 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 6:1-8 | mark: a white horse; another horse that was red; a black horse; a pale horse
p: The first four seals depict tribulation’s trials (war, famine, death).

--- Ye shall be hated
kicker: 1 · Scriptures
scripture: Matthew 24:6-9 | mark: ye shall be hated of all nations for my name’s sake
p: Believers endure tribulation.
callout: **Why:** The church’s presence ([[Matthew 24:9]], “ye”) and seals’ trials (Revelation 6) define tribulation as distinct from wrath. Pre-tribulationism’s claim that the church is absent ignores these scriptures.

=== 2. Midpoint
--- Midpoint: Abomination of Desolation and Beast’s Empowerment
kicker: 2 · ~1260 Days
p: **Description:** At the 7-year midpoint, the beast breaks the covenant, halts sacrifices, and sets up the abomination of desolation, triggering the great tribulation. The beast suffers a deadly head wound, is healed (possibly empowered/possessed by the dragon), and begins its 42-month reign, intensifying persecution.
p: **Key Events:**
- Abomination of desolation desecrates the temple.
- Beast’s head wound is healed, gaining global worship.
- Dragon empowers the beast, starting its 42-month authority.

--- The abomination of desolation
kicker: 2 · Scriptures
scripture: Matthew 24:15; Matthew 24:21 | mark: When ye therefore shall see the abomination of desolation; then shall be great tribulation
p: The church (“ye”) faces great tribulation.
xr: Daniel 9:27 | The abomination marks the midpoint.
xr: 2 Thessalonians 2:4 | This parallels the abomination.

--- The deadly wound healed
kicker: 2 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 13:2-5 | mark: the dragon gave him his power; his deadly wound was healed; power was given unto him to continue forty and two months
p: The wound and dragon’s power ([[Revelation 13:2]]) initiate the beast’s reign.
callout: **Why:** The abomination ([[Daniel 9:27]]) and beast’s wound ([[Revelation 13:3]]) trigger great tribulation, with saints present ([[Matthew 24:15]], [[Revelation 13:7]]). Pre-tribulationism’s early rapture contradicts this.

=== 3. The 75 days
--- 75 Days: Climactic Great Tribulation
kicker: 3 · ~1260 to ~1335 Days
p: **Description:** The great tribulation’s climax, a 75-day period post-abomination and beast’s wound, is the most intense phase of persecution, “cut short” for the elect. The beast enforces the mark and image worship, warring against saints, until cosmic signs herald Christ’s return and the rapture. The 75 days derive from [[Daniel 12:11-12]]’s 1290-1335 days.
p: **Key Events:**
- Beast enforces mark and image worship, persecuting saints.
- Great tribulation “cut short” to preserve the elect.
- Cosmic signs (sun darkened, stars fall) signal tribulation’s end.
- Rapture at Christ’s visible second coming (~1290 days).

--- The 1290 and 1335 days
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Daniel 12:11-12 | mark: a thousand two hundred and ninety days; the thousand three hundred and five and thirty days
p: The 1290 days may mark the rapture; 1335 days, a later blessing (e.g., kingdom).

--- War with the saints
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 13:7; Revelation 13:15-17 | mark: make war with the saints; as many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed
p: The beast’s persecution peaks.

--- Those days shortened
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Matthew 24:22; Matthew 24:24 | mark: for the elect’s sake those days shall be shortened; if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect
p: The tribulation is cut short, with the elect present.

--- The sixth seal
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 6:12-17 | mark: the sun became black as sackcloth of hair; the wrath of the Lamb
p: Cosmic signs match [[Matthew 24:29]].

--- Immediately after the tribulation
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Matthew 24:29-31 | mark: Immediately after the tribulation of those days; they shall gather together his elect
p: The rapture occurs post-tribulation.

--- Out of great tribulation
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 7:9-14 | mark: a great multitude; These are they which came out of great tribulation
p: The multitude is raptured post-tribulation.

--- On the sea of glass
kicker: 3 · Scriptures
big: Revelation 15:2 | mark: them that had gotten the victory over the beast
p: These saints, post-75 days, parallel Revelation 7’s multitude.
callout: **Why:** The 75-day climax ([[Daniel 12:11-12]]) aligns with the beast’s persecution ([[Revelation 13:7]]) and cosmic signs ([[Revelation 6:12]]), ending with the rapture ([[Matthew 24:31]]). The church’s presence refutes pre-tribulationism, as saints endure the mark and deception ([[Matthew 24:24]]). Revelation’s parallel accounts place this in both 6-7 and 13-15. **The beast’s full 42-month reign continues through the subsequent wrath period.**

=== 4. Half hour of silence
--- Half Hour of Silence: Transition to Wrath
kicker: 4 · ~1290 Days
p: **Description:** After the rapture, a brief pause in heaven marks the shift from tribulation to God’s wrath, as the seventh seal is opened.
p: **Key Event:**
- Silence in heaven, preparing for judgments.
big: Revelation 8:1
callout: **Why:** The silence follows the sixth seal’s rapture ([[Revelation 6:12-17]]), distinguishing tribulation from wrath. The church, now raptured, is spared wrath ([[1 Thessalonians 5:9]]).

=== 5. Wrath
--- Wrath: Trumpets and Vials
kicker: 5 · ~1290 to ~1335 Days or Beyond
p: **Description:** God’s wrath, post-rapture, targets the beast’s kingdom via trumpets and vials, which are parallel judgments in Revelation’s two accounts (4-11 and 12-22). The beast and his followers endure these supernatural judgments.
p: **Key Events:**
- Trumpets afflict the earth (third part affected).
- Vials intensify judgments (universal scope).
- Beast’s kingdom suffers, gathers for Armageddon.

--- The first trumpet and the first vial
kicker: 5 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 8:7; Revelation 16:2 | mark: the third part of trees was burnt up; a noisome and grievous sore upon the men which had the mark of the beast

--- The beast’s kingdom
kicker: 5 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 16:10; Revelation 16:13-14 | mark: his kingdom was full of darkness; to gather them to the battle of that great day of God Almighty

--- Not appointed to wrath
kicker: 5 · Scriptures
big: 1 Thessalonians 5:9
callout: **Why:** Trumpets and vials, as parallel wrath (Revelation 8-9, 16), follow the rapture, targeting the beast’s followers ([[Revelation 16:2]]). The church’s absence during wrath aligns with the tribulation/wrath distinction, refuting pre-tribulationism’s conflation. **The beast continues his reign throughout this period.**

=== 6. Christ’s return
--- Christ’s Return with Glorified Saints and Millennial Kingdom
kicker: 6 · ~1335 Days or Later
p: **Description:** After wrath, Christ returns with glorified saints (raptured earlier) to defeat the beast and false prophet, bind Satan, and establish the 1,000-year kingdom.
p: **Key Events:**
- Christ returns with saints, defeats the beast.
- Beast and false prophet cast into the lake of fire.
- Satan bound for 1,000 years.
- Millennial kingdom established.

--- The armies which were in heaven
kicker: 6 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 19:11-14; Revelation 19:20 | mark: the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses; These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone

--- Bound a thousand years
kicker: 6 · Scriptures
scripture: Revelation 20:1-6 | mark: bound him a thousand years; they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years
refs: Daniel 7:27
xr: Revelation 11:15 | This parallels Revelation 19 in the 4-11 account.
callout: **Why:** Christ’s return with saints (Revelation 19) follows wrath, fulfilling the kingdom’s establishment ([[Revelation 11:15]], [[Revelation 20:4]]). The church, raptured post-tribulation, returns glorified, aligning with this view.

=== Refutation
--- Refutation of Pre-Tribulationism
p: This timeline counters pre-tribulationism’s errors:
panel: Church’s Presence | Saints endure tribulation ([[Revelation 13:7]], [[Matthew 24:24]]), facing the beast’s mark and abomination, contradicting an early rapture.
panel: Visible Rapture | The rapture at Christ’s second coming ([[Matthew 24:29-31]], [[Revelation 6:12-17]]) is visible ([[Revelation 1:7]]), not secret.
panel-warn: Tribulation vs. Wrath | Tribulation (persecution, disasters) is distinct from wrath (God’s judgments), with the church enduring the former (Revelation 6-7, 13) but spared the latter (Revelation 8-9, 16).
panel: No Invented Doctrines | “Saints” ([[Revelation 7:14]], [[Revelation 13:7]]) are the church, not a separate “tribulation saints” group, aligning with a plain reading.

=== Conclusion
--- Conclusion
lead: This post-tribulation, pre-wrath timeline, rooted in Daniel’s 7-year framework and Revelation’s parallel accounts, places the church in tribulation (3.5 years, 75-day climax), raptured at Christ’s visible second coming (~1290 days), spared wrath (trumpets/vials), and returning with Christ to establish the millennium.
callout: The 75-day climactic great tribulation, post-abomination and beast’s wound, is a pivotal period of intense persecution, cut short for the elect.

--- Chronological Timeline: tribulation
kicker: Chronological Timeline Table (Visual Summary)
step: Days 1–1260 (~3.5 yrs) | **Beginning of Sorrows.** Seals 1–5/6: Conquest, war, famine, death, martyrdom. Church endures. [[Matthew 24:4-14]] [[Revelation 6:1-11]]
step: Day 1260 | **Midpoint.** Abomination of desolation; beast’s wound healed; dragon empowers beast. [[Daniel 9:27]] [[Matthew 24:15]] [[Revelation 13:1-5]]
step: Days 1261 – ~1335 (~75 days) | **Climactic Great Tribulation.** Mark enforced, war on saints peaks, persecution at maximum intensity. Days “cut short” for the elect. [[Matthew 24:21-22]] [[Revelation 13:7-17]] [[Daniel 12:11-12]]

--- Chronological Timeline: rapture and wrath
kicker: Chronological Timeline Table (Visual Summary)
step: ~Day 1335 | **Rapture & Cosmic Signs.** Sun/moon darkened, stars fall, Son of Man appears, angels gather elect. [[Matthew 24:29-31]] Revelation 6:12–7:17
step: Brief transition | **Half-hour silence.** Seventh seal opened → pause in heaven. [[Revelation 8:1]]
step: Remaining ~1185 days | **God’s Wrath (Day of the Lord).** Trumpets & vials poured out on beast’s kingdom while beast still reigns (full 42 months). Revelation 8–9, 16 · [[1 Thessalonians 5:9]]
step: Day 2520 | **End of 7 Years.** Christ returns with saints, beast/false prophet defeated, Satan bound, millennial kingdom begins. Revelation 19–20

=== The Olivet Discourse
--- Pronoun Usage and Timing Clauses in the Olivet Discourse
kicker: Matthew 24, Mark 13, Luke 21 (KJV)
p: The table below analyzes key verses from the Olivet Discourse, focusing on **timing clauses** (e.g., “before,” “then,” “after,” “immediately after,” “in those days”) and **pronoun shifts** (“ye/you/your” for believers Jesus addresses directly vs. “they/them” for unbelieving world/Jews or general unbelievers). This supports the premise:
- Believers (“ye”) endure general tribulation (beginning of sorrows) and the climactic great tribulation (post-abomination, cut short).
- The rapture gathers the elect immediately after this tribulation.
- Unbelievers (“they”) face ongoing wrath/judgment post-rapture (beast’s reign continues, but church is spared).

--- Olivet Discourse: the beginning of sorrows
kicker: Pronoun Usage and Timing Clauses
group: **Beginning phase** (before the end). **“Ye”** (believers addressed) | **General tribulation (first 3.5 years):** Church endures wars, famines, earthquakes as “beginning of sorrows.” | Matthew 24:6-8; Mark 13:7-8; Luke 21:9-11
group: **“Then”** (after beginning of sorrows). Luke: *“before all these”* (persecution precedes some signs). **Shift:** **“They”** deliver/persecute; **“you/ye”** (believers) are victims | **General tribulation:** Believers persecuted/hated; church present and enduring. | Matthew 24:9; Mark 13:9; Mark 13:13; Luke 21:12; Luke 21:17
group: **“When ye shall see”** (midpoint trigger). **“Ye”** (believers see and respond) | **Midpoint:** Abomination triggers climactic great tribulation; believers witness it and are instructed to flee. | Matthew 24:15; Mark 13:14; Luke 21:20

--- Olivet Discourse: great tribulation
kicker: Pronoun Usage and Timing Clauses
group: **“Then”** / **“For in those days”** (immediately post-abomination). Luke: **“This people”** (unbelieving Jews); general affliction | **Climactic great tribulation (75 days):** Intense phase begins; Luke highlights wrath/vengeance on unbelieving Israel (“days of vengeance”). | Matthew 24:21; Mark 13:19; Luke 21:23
group: **Shortening of “those days.”** **“The elect”** (believers) | **Climactic great tribulation cut short** (~75 days via Daniel 12); preserves believers for rapture. | Matthew 24:22; Mark 13:20
group: **During great tribulation.** **“They”** (false prophets deceive); **“the very elect”** (believers protected) | **Church (“elect”) present** during deception but not deceived. | Matthew 24:24; Mark 13:22

--- Olivet Discourse: after that tribulation
kicker: Pronoun Usage and Timing Clauses
group: **“Immediately after”** / **“after that tribulation”** / *“those things which are coming on the earth.”* **“Men’s hearts”** / general fear (unbelievers) | **End of climactic great tribulation:** Cosmic signs; unbelievers (“they/men”) terrified as wrath approaches. | Matthew 24:29; Mark 13:24; Luke 21:25-26
group: **“Immediately after… And then”** / *“And then shall they see.”* **Shift:** **“All the tribes… they”** mourn/see (unbelievers); angels gather **“his elect”** / **“your redemption”** (believers) | **Rapture at visible second coming:** Unbelievers mourn; elect (church/believers) gathered/raptured post-tribulation, pre-full wrath. | Matthew 24:30-31; Mark 13:26-27; Luke 21:27-28
group: **“In those days”** (great tribulation/wrath overlap for unbelievers). **“This people… they”** (unbelieving Jews) | **Supports distinction:** Unbelieving Israel endures “days of vengeance”/wrath (beast’s persecution continues post-rapture). | Luke 21:23-24

--- What the Olivet table shows
kicker: Pronoun Usage and Timing Clauses
lead: This table demonstrates how Jesus’ **timing clauses** sequence events into general tribulation → midpoint trigger → shortened climactic great tribulation → immediate cosmic signs/rapture.
p: **Pronoun shifts** consistently address believers (“ye/you”) for endurance and deliverance, while “they/them” describes unbelievers (especially unbelieving Jews in context) facing mourning, fear, and vengeance. Supporting the view that the church/believer endures tribulation but is raptured pre-wrath, with the beast’s reign persisting against the unsaved through the wrath.

=== Revelation’s two accounts
--- Parallel Structure of Revelation
kicker: Overlapping Accounts (Chapters 4-11 and 12-22)
p: Revelation uses recapitulation: the same timeline is repeated from heavenly (4-11) and cosmic/earthly (12-22) perspectives. The rapture is at the sixth seal ([[Revelation 6:12-17]]), with saints immediately appearing in heaven ([[Revelation 7:9-17]], paralleled in [[Revelation 15:2]]).
image: lessons/prophecy/revelation-parallel-accounts.svg | Revelation 4 to 11 beside Revelation 12 to 22, phase by phase: throne room and Lamb beside the dragon cast out; seals 1 to 5 beside the beast rising; the sixth seal beside the mark, image and war on saints; the great multitude beside the sea of glass; the half-hour silence beside the temple filled with smoke; the trumpets beside the vials; the seventh trumpet beside Christ’s return | Same events, different angles

--- Heavenly Introduction / Start of Conflict
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 1
panel: Rev 4-5 (Heavenly Perspective) | Throne room; Lamb worthy to open scroll. *Details* ([[Revelation 4:1-11]]; [[Revelation 5:1-14]]): Door open in heaven; Lamb takes scroll; worship.
panel: Rev 12 (Cosmic/Earthly Perspective) | Dragon, woman, child, war in heaven. *Details* ([[Revelation 12:1-12]]): Woman clothed with sun; dragon cast out; rejoicing in heaven.
p: **Overlap:** Heavenly authority given; cosmic war begins as Satan is cast down.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Daniel 7:9-14]] (throne, books opened); [[John 12:31]].

--- General Tribulation (Beginning of Sorrows)
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 2
panel: Rev 6:1-11: Seals 1-5 opened | White (conquest), Red (war), Black (famine), Pale (death) horses; martyrs under altar ([[Revelation 6:9-11|v. 9-11]]).
panel: Rev 13:1-10: Beast from sea rises, wars on saints | Beast with heads/horns; authority 42 months; overcomes saints.
p: **Overlap:** Man/Satan-driven trials: wars, famine, death, persecution; church endures.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Matthew 24:4-14]] (wars, famines); [[Luke 21:9-12]]; [[Revelation 13:7]].

--- Midpoint Trigger & Climactic Great Tribulation
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 3
panel: Rev 6:12-17: 6th Seal – Cosmic disturbance | Earthquake; sun black, moon blood, stars fall; kings hide from “wrath of the Lamb.”
panel: Rev 13: Beast fully empowered; mark, image, persecution | Beast’s wound healed; dragon gives power; war on saints; mark 666 enforced.
p: **Overlap:** Abomination/beast empowerment triggers intense persecution (“cut short” for elect); cosmic signs end this phase.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Daniel 9:27]] (abomination); [[Matthew 24:15-22]], [[Matthew 24:29]]; [[Daniel 12:11-12]] (1290/1335 days).

--- Rapture & Saints in Heaven
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 4
panel: Rev 7:1-17: Multitude from great tribulation before throne | 144,000 sealed; great multitude from all nations; God wipes away tears.
panel: Rev 15:2: Victors over beast on sea of glass | *Details* ([[Revelation 15:1-8]]): Sea of glass mingled with fire; harps; song of Moses/Lamb.
p: **Overlap:** Raptured church safe in heaven post-tribulation; victory over beast/mark.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Matthew 24:29-31]]; [[1 Thessalonians 4:16-17]]; [[Revelation 6:12-17]].

--- Transition to Wrath
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 5
panel: Rev 8:1: Half-hour silence when 7th seal opened | Silence in heaven about half an hour.
panel: Implicit transition after victors appear in heaven | *Details* ([[Revelation 15:5-8]]): Temple filled with smoke; no man enters till plagues finished.
p: **Overlap:** Brief heavenly pause before judgments begin.

--- God’s Wrath Poured Out
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 6
panel-warn: Rev 8-9: Trumpets – Partial judgments | Hail/fire, sea blood, waters bitter (thirds affected); locusts/demonic army.
panel-warn: Rev 16: Vials – Intensified/universal judgments | Sores on mark-bearers, sea/rivers blood, darkness on kingdom, Armageddon gathered.
p: **Overlap:** Parallel wrath: Trumpets affect thirds (partial); vials full/universal on beast’s kingdom.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Joel 2:1-11]]; [[Revelation 16:2]], [[Revelation 16:10-11]] (target mark-bearers); [[1 Thessalonians 5:9]].

--- Kingdom Proclaimed / Established
kicker: Parallel Structure of Revelation · 7
panel: Rev 11:15-19: 7th trumpet – Kingdom comes | Kingdoms become Christ’s; reward saints, destroy destroyers.
panel: Rev 19-20: Christ returns, beast defeated, millennium | White horse return; beast to lake of fire; Satan bound; saints reign 1000 years.
p: **Overlap:** Final victory; kingdom established.
p: **Key cross-references:** [[Daniel 7:27]]; [[Matthew 25:31-46]]; [[Revelation 11:15]] // Revelation 19.
callout: This detailed table reinforces the parallel structure: same events (tribulation → rapture → wrath → kingdom), different angles. The church endures tribulation (Rev 6 seals / Rev 13 beast) but is raptured at the sixth seal before wrath (Rev 8+ trumpets // Rev 16 vials).

=== Trumpets and vials
--- Trumpets and Vials as Parallel Judgments in Revelation
p: The trumpets (Rev 8–9) and vials/bowls (Rev 16) are **parallel descriptions of the same wrath judgments** from different perspectives:
- **Trumpets:** Heavenly viewpoint, partial/limited scope (often “a third” affected), emphasizing warning and opportunity for repentance (though none repent, [[Revelation 9:20-21|Rev 9:20-21]]).
- **Vials:** Earthly/cosmic viewpoint, intensified/universal scope, poured out on the beast’s kingdom and mark-bearers specifically.
p: This supports the overlapping structure (Rev 4-11 heavenly // Rev 12-22 earthly), with wrath post-rapture targeting the ungodly while the church is absent.

--- Seven trumpets, seven vials
kicker: Trumpets and Vials as Parallel Judgments
table: Trumpet (Rev 8–9) | Vial/Bowl (Rev 16)
tr: **1st** · Rev 8:7 – Hail and fire mingled with blood | **1st** · Rev 16:2 – Noisome and grievous sore
tr: **2nd** · Rev 8:8-9 – Great mountain burning with fire cast into sea | **2nd** · Rev 16:3 – Vial poured into sea
tr: **3rd** · Rev 8:10-11 – Great star (Wormwood) falls, burns | **3rd** · Rev 16:4-7 – Vial into rivers and fountains
tr: **4th** · Rev 8:12 – Heavens smitten | **4th** · Rev 16:8-9 – Vial upon the sun
tr: **5th** · Rev 9:1-12 – Star falls, opens bottomless pit; locusts torment | **5th** · Rev 16:10-11 – Vial upon throne of beast
tr: **6th** · Rev 9:13-21 – Four angels loosed at Euphrates; 200M horsemen | **6th** · Rev 16:12-16 – Vial upon Euphrates
tr: **7th** · Rev 11:15-19 – Great voices: kingdoms become Christ’s | **7th** · Rev 16:17-21 – Vial into air; “It is done”

--- The 1st trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 1st
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 8:7]] | Burns a third of trees, all green grass.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:2]] | Sores on men who have the mark of the beast and worship his image.
p: **Parallel:** Earth afflicted (vegetation burned // sores on beast followers).
p: **Note:** Targeted at beast system in vials.

--- The 2nd trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 2nd
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 8:8-9]] | Third of sea becomes blood; third of sea creatures die; third of ships destroyed.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:3]] | Sea becomes blood as of a dead man; every living soul in sea dies.
p: **Parallel:** Sea turned to blood (partial // total).
p: **Note:** Escalation from warning to full judgment.

--- The 3rd trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 3rd
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 8:10-11]] | Third of rivers/fountains bitter; many men die from waters.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:4-7]] | Rivers/fountains become blood; angel declares righteousness.
p: **Parallel:** Fresh waters poisoned/blood (partial // total).
p: **Note:** Judgment on water sources.

--- The 4th trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 4th
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 8:12]] | Third of sun, moon, stars darkened; third of day/night no light.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:8-9]] | Sun scorches men with fire; men blaspheme God, repent not.
p: **Parallel:** Heavenly lights afflicted (partial darkening // intensified heat).
p: **Note:** Men gnaw tongues but do not repent.

--- The 5th trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 5th
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 9:1-12]] | Torment men without seal of God for 5 months (no death); like scorpions.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:10-11]] | Kingdom full of darkness; men gnaw tongues for pain, blaspheme God.
p: **Parallel:** Darkness and torment (demonic locusts // darkness on beast throne).
p: **Note:** Pain without repentance; beast targeted.

--- The 6th trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 6th
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 9:13-21]] | Third of men killed by fire/smoke/brimstone; no repentance of idolatry/murder.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:12-16]] | River dried for kings of east; unclean spirits gather to Armageddon.
p: **Parallel:** Euphrates involved; demonic gathering/armies (killing third // gathering for final battle).
p: **Note:** Preparation for Armageddon.

--- The 7th trumpet and vial
kicker: Trumpets and Vials · 7th
panel: Trumpet · [[Revelation 11:15-19]] | Temple opened, lightning, voices, earthquake, hail.
panel-warn: Vial · [[Revelation 16:17-21]] | Voices, thunders, greatest earthquake, Babylon falls, great hail.
p: **Parallel:** Final consummation: kingdom proclaimed // great earthquake/hail, Babylon judged.
p: **Note:** [[Revelation 11:15]]; parallels Rev 19-20 kingdom.
callout: This parallelism shows trumpets as limited warnings (partial, heavenly focus) and vials as complete execution (universal, earthly focus on beast worshippers). Both occur post-rapture during the wrath period, with the beast active throughout ([[Revelation 16:10]], [[Revelation 16:13-14]]). No repentance in either ([[Revelation 9:20-21]]; [[Revelation 16:9]], [[Revelation 16:11]]). Supports [[1 Thessalonians 5:9]]—church spared wrath.

=== Close
--- Tribulation, Rapture, Wrath, Kingdom [title]
overline: Prophecy & the covenants
heading: Tribulation, Rapture, Wrath, Kingdom
sub: Same events (tribulation → rapture → wrath → kingdom), different angles.
point: Tribulation | The church endures tribulation (Rev 6 seals / Rev 13 beast). [[Matthew 24:9]]
point: Rapture | Raptured at Christ’s visible second coming. [[Matthew 24:29-31]]
point: Wrath | Spared wrath (trumpets/vials). [[1 Thessalonians 5:9]]
point: Kingdom | Returning with Christ to establish the millennium. [[Revelation 19:11-14]]
